PART I - ENGLISH OFFICIAL LICENSE (INTERNATIONAL EDITION)

ARTICLE 01 - SCOPE OF OWNERSHIP & INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
All original engineering, visual design, and curated digital assets integrated
within KELIR are the proprietary intellectual property of Nawfal Irfan,
including without limitation:
1. Application source code written in Svelte 5, TypeScript, HTML, and CSS,
   including the Washi Alabaster (Light) and Smoked Obsidian (Dark) UI systems.
2. Three.js WebGL spatial stages and procedural 3D geometry builders (Living
   Pendopo Diorama, Besalen Empu, Bale Karawitan, Digital Twin CAD, 3D
   Coverflow, Pakeliran Shadow Stage, Suluk Altar, and Pamomong Astrolabe),
   together with procedural canvas textures and offscreen studio renderers.
3. Client-side Web Audio API acoustic engines synthesizing Gamelan instruments
   and 8 classical Javanese Karawitan repertoires.
4. Architecture and orchestration of the Pamomong Nusantara AI agent, local BM25
   retrieval engine, layered anti-injection guardrails, and 6 AI Studio modes.
5. The 86-character Hanacaraka Javanese script engine (Unicode U+A980-U+A9DF),
   4-language localization matrix (ID/EN/JW/AKS), PNG Curator Certificate
   generator, adaptive cursor module, and technical documentation.

ARTICLE 02 - COMMUNAL CULTURAL HERITAGE & PRIMARY ATTRIBUTION (S1-S7)
This Personal License DOES NOT assert private or exclusive ownership over the
historical knowledge, traditional philosophies, puppetry conventions, musical
tunings, architecture traditions, or regional scripts of Indonesia. All
communal heritage knowledge belongs to the public and cultural communities, and
is transparently attributed to official archival sources S1 through S7:
- S1: UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage (Indonesian Keris)
- S2: UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage (Indonesian Batik)
- S3: UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage (Wayang Puppet Theatre)
- S4: UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage (Gamelan)
- S5: Museum Sonobudoyo & ISI Surakarta (Ramayana Shadow Theatre Studies)
- S6: Ministry of Culture of the Republic of Indonesia / Kemdikbudristek RI
      (Pendopo Joglo & Tumpang Sari Vernacular Architecture)
- S7: Javanese Language Congress, National Library of Indonesia (Perpusnas RI),
      & the Unicode Consortium (Javanese Script Block U+A980-U+A9DF)

